Spexis is a fork of vLLM v0.8.4 (commit dc1b4a6f1300003ae27f033afbdff5e2683721ce).
The following modifications were made to the original software:

  * Added vllm/specpipe/, which implements speculative pipeline
    parallelism: an early-exit draft model per pipeline stage, a
    scheduler that overlaps speculation with normal execution and
    verifies it one iteration later, confidence-based speculation
    dropping, and lookahead scheduling based on predicted generation
    length and KV-cache pressure.
  * Integrated the above into the V1 engine (engine core, scheduler
    output, request state, GPU model runner and worker, Ray executor).
    Modified regions in upstream files are marked with "[Spexis]".
  * Removed support for non-CUDA platforms, models other than the Llama
    and Qwen families used by the paper, V0 speculative decoding, and
    the CUDA kernel sources (this fork is Python-only and installs
    against the prebuilt upstream vLLM v0.8.4 wheel).

Files that are unmodified from vLLM retain their original copyright and
license headers.
